<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements of the COMPANY build of the app (scripts/build_pkg.sh with an app identity signs a copy of the app with them,
  with the hardened runtime and a secure timestamp). The personal build (scripts/build_app.sh, self-signed identity) has no hardened
  runtime and no entitlements and does not use this file. Passing this file is an administrator action together with the Developer ID identity.

  Only what the app really does is listed. Under the hardened runtime everything else is refused:

  com.apple.security.device.audio-input
      The microphone track (mic.wav). The hardened runtime blocks microphone capture without it. The permission prompt itself is still the
      Microphone entry of System Settings > Privacy & Security (NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist).

  com.apple.security.automation.apple-events
      Sending Apple Events to Google Chrome: only used when ENABLED_PLATFORMS contains meet (the app reads the address and title of Meet
      tabs). The company install does not enable meet, but the code path is part of the binary and would fail silently without the
      entitlement (NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist). Remove this key from the file if the organisation never wants Meet.

  Deliberately NOT here: com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory, disable-library-validation,
  disable-executable-page-protection, get-task-allow, and every com.apple.security.app-sandbox key (the app is not sandboxed: it starts the
  pipeline, reads the Drive folder and writes under ~/Library). The Python pipeline is a child process with its own signature, not code that
  this app loads, so no library-validation exception is needed.

  System audio (the "System Audio Recording" permission, Core Audio Process Tap) is a TCC permission without an entitlement of its own.
  [미검증] Whether Process Tap capture works under the hardened runtime with exactly these entitlements has to be tested on a device
  (docs/LIVE_TEST.md, administrator action) before any rollout; macOS asks for Microphone and System Audio Recording again because the signing
  identity changes (docs/MIGRATION.md).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
